# Verify visually

There is no test runner in this repo. A clean type-check proves nothing about a
UI change. **Run the app and look at it.**

## The loop

```bash
pnpm dev --port <a free port>
```

Then capture the affected routes at **1280 and 390**, in **light and dark**,
before and after your change. A change that looks right at 1280 in light and
breaks at 390 in dark is the normal failure here, not the rare one.

A ready-made capture script lives at
`.claude/skills/blog-post/scripts/screenshot.mjs`. It drives headless Chrome
through the DevTools Protocol — plain CLI flags are not enough, because headless
Chrome clamps the window and follows the OS colour scheme. It also warns on
horizontal overflow, which is the failure mode this codebase actually hits.

```bash
node .claude/skills/blog-post/scripts/screenshot.mjs http://localhost:<port>/notes/<slug> <outDir>
```

Kill the dev server when you are done.

## Routes worth checking

| You touched | Capture |
|---|---|
| tokens, `global.css` | `/`, `/notes`, a note, a series landing |
| note components | the notes that import them, at both widths |
| series | `/notes/series/agent-vs-cursor` and `/claude-certified-architect` |
| listings | `/notes`, `/es/notes`, `/notes/archive` |
| CV | `/`, `/cv`, plus a print preview |

## Report honestly

State what you checked and what you did not. If a criterion is unmet, say so
with the evidence — do not round it up to done. If something outside your ticket
is broken, note it and leave it alone.
